> The wizard's pages. Each one opens the next; Esc (back) returns to the
> page below it on the stack.

menu WELCOME context POPUP
- NEXT open PROFILE
- CANCEL close

> A form (spec §8.1): Tab moves between the fields, Enter checks them
> all and stores them at once, then the next page opens.
panel PROFILE then open OPTIONS
[lname_____] [name______________________]
[lemail____] [email_____________________]
[lpass_____] [pass______________________]
[ledition__] [edition___________________]
legend:
- lname text PROFILE.NAME
- name input NAME_IN
- lemail text PROFILE.EMAIL
- email input EMAIL_IN
- lpass text PROFILE.PASSWORD
- pass input PASSWORD_IN
- ledition text PROFILE.EDITION
- edition input EDITION_IN

input NAME_IN
- var NAME
- validate $VALUE != ""
- error PROFILE.NAME_EMPTY

input EMAIL_IN
- var EMAIL
- validate ok $(printf '%s' "$VALUE" | grep -q '^[^@ ]*@[^@ ]*\.[^@ ]*$')
- error PROFILE.EMAIL_BAD

> A password is never echoed or logged; INSTALL gets it on stdin.
input PASSWORD_IN
- var PASSWORD
- kind password

> A choice field: the arrow keys change the value.
input EDITION_IN
- var EDITION
- kind choice

> toggle flips a bool, adjust steps a number within its range.
menu OPTIONS context POPUP
- VERBOSE toggle VERBOSE
- WORKERS adjust WORKERS 1..8
- NEXT open THEME_PICKER
- BACK back

> A grid with a cursor (spec §5.1): the arrow keys pick a cell, Enter
> runs PICK_THEME with the cursor in THEME_ROW and THEME_COL.
panel THEME_PICKER
tttttttttttttttttttttttttttt
cccccccc cccccccc cccccccc
cccccccc cccccccc cccccccc

legend:
- t text THEME_PICKER.HINT
- c grid $(printf '\033[36mocean\033[0m \033[32mforest\033[0m \033[33msand\033[0m\n\033[35mberry\033[0m \033[31member\033[0m \033[37mmono\033[0m') ansi cursor THEME_ROW THEME_COL then PICK_THEME

> A path with completion: Tab completes, a second Tab lists the matches.
input TARGET_DIR
- var TARGET
- kind path
- validate ok $(test -d "$(dirname "$VALUE")")
- error TARGET_DIR.INVALID
- then open PART_LIST

> A list menu with columns: type to filter, Insert marks several rows,
> Enter goes on with the marked rows (or the row under the cursor) as IT.
> A row's commands get the row as IT too.
menu PART_LIST list
- source $(printf '%s\n' "core 12" "docs 4" "examples 3" "fonts 25" "themes 1" "tools 8")
- columns PART:14 SIZE:6 right
- row PART: $(echo "$IT" | cut -d' ' -f1) SIZE: $(echo "$IT" | cut -d' ' -f2)
- filter
- multi
- then CHOOSE_PARTS

menu CONFIRM context POPUP
- INSTALL
- BACK back
- CANCEL close

menu DONE context POPUP
- VIEW
- SHELL
- FINISH close

> `final`: Esc does not close it; the user must pick an item that leaves
> it (open or quit).
menu FAILED context POPUP final
- RETRY open CONFIRM
- QUIT quit
